From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn: wire the headset to the USBSS

The board's headphone lines run through the WCD9395 USB-SS analog
switch, but nothing said so: the codec had no port graph at all, and the
switch's own headset endpoint was declared and left dangling.

wcd939x decides whether the headset is muxed by looking for exactly that
link:

	np = of_graph_get_remote_node(dev->of_node, 0, 0);
	if (np) {
		wcd939x->typec_analog_mux = true;
		cfg->typec_analog_mux = true;
		cfg->swap_gnd_mic = wcd939x_swap_gnd_mic;
	}

With no remote node it never sets typec_analog_mux, never acquires the
switch through fwnode_typec_switch_get(), and so never has the USBSS
route the headset lines. On an Odin 3 that means plugging headphones in
does nothing audible: MBHC's mechanical interrupt fires, but "Elect
Insert" never does, "Headphone Jack" stays off, and userspace is never
told to move away from the speaker.

Wire both ends the way sm8750-mtp does - the codec node here is
otherwise identical to the MTP's, down to the micbias levels, the MBHC
thresholds and the reset GPIO - and add the mode-switch and
orientation-switch properties that go with being part of the Type-C mux
chain.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
@@ -49,6 +49,15 @@
 		vdd-px-supply = <&vreg_l2i_1p2>;

 		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
+
+		mode-switch;
+		orientation-switch;
+
+		port {
+			wcd_codec_headset_in: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&wcd_usbss_headset_out>;
+			};
+		};
 	};

 	chosen {
@@ -861,6 +870,7 @@
 				reg = <1>;

 				wcd_usbss_headset_out: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&wcd_codec_headset_in>;
 				};
 			};
 		};
